  "documentReadinessSectionTitle": "Document readiness before the move",
  "documentReadinessPriorityCritical": "Critical now",
  "documentReadinessPriorityPrepare": "Prepare with lead time",
  "documentReadinessPriorityArrival": "Keep ready on arrival",
  "documentReadinessSummaryResearching": "Before comparing too many paths, make sure your move depends on a document pack that can actually be assembled without surprises.",
  "documentReadinessSummaryTwelveMonths": "With more time, the goal is to remove preventable document risk early instead of discovering missing items close to the move.",
  "documentReadinessSummarySixMonths": "Six months is enough to organize the hard documents now and leave the arrival layer lighter.",
  "documentReadinessSummaryAsap": "Since the move is close, focus on the documents that can block residency, banking, and housing before anything else.",
  "documentReadinessRouteTitle": "Validate the legal entry route",
  "documentReadinessRouteBodyBrazil": "Confirm whether your move will rely on the Mercosur residence path and what that route demands before you book around assumptions.",
  "documentReadinessRouteBodyGeneric": "Confirm the legal route for the destination first so the rest of the checklist is built on the correct migration path.",
  "documentReadinessIdentityPackTitle": "Separate the core identity pack",
  "documentReadinessIdentityPackBody": "Keep passport, birth records, criminal records, and personal identifiers in one reviewed bundle before opening other fronts.",
  "documentReadinessApostilleTitle": "Review apostille and validity windows",
  "documentReadinessApostilleBodyBrazil": "For Brazil, check which Argentine documents need apostille, how recent they must be, and what can expire before arrival.",
  "documentReadinessRuleCheckTitle": "Check official document rules early",
  "documentReadinessRuleCheckBody": "Map which documents must be original, apostilled, translated, or issued again so the move does not depend on assumptions.",
  "documentReadinessTranslationTitle": "Map translation needs before paying twice",
  "documentReadinessTranslationBodyBrazil": "Separate what can stay in Spanish from what may require sworn translation in Brazil, especially for residency and civil proof.",
  "documentReadinessTranslationBodyGeneric": "Separate what can remain in the source language from what may require certified translation in the destination country.",
  "documentReadinessHousingProofTitle": "Prepare proof for housing and routine setup",
  "documentReadinessHousingProofBodyBrazil": "Group proof of income, reserve, identification, and any supporting papers that landlords, banks, or guarantee products may ask for in Brazil.",
  "documentReadinessProofPackTitle": "Build your practical proof pack",
  "documentReadinessProofPackBody": "Group identity, proof of funds, income evidence, and the documents that usually unlock banking, housing, and essential services.",
  "documentReadinessCpfTitle": "Treat CPF and regular status as one layer",
  "documentReadinessCpfBodyBrazil": "CPF, residency follow-up, and your first local proof often unlock the practical side of arrival. Keep that bundle ready to execute fast.",
  "documentReadinessCopiesTitle": "Keep physical and digital backups aligned",
  "documentReadinessCopiesBody": "Save scans, originals, and emergency copies in a structure that can be accessed from your phone and used in person if needed.",
  "documentReadinessArrivalFolderTitle": "Prepare an arrival folder, not scattered files",
  "documentReadinessArrivalFolderBodyBrazil": "Create one arrival folder with residency follow-up, CPF references, address notes, and the proof most likely to be requested in the first month.",
  "documentReadinessArrivalFolderBodyGeneric": "Create one arrival folder with the first documents, local proof notes, and the evidence you are most likely to need in the first weeks.",
  "documentReadinessGoalWorkTitle": "Protect your employability documents",
  "documentReadinessGoalWorkBodyBrazil": "Review what can block early work in Brazil: identity consistency, residence follow-up, and any profession-specific proof you may need to show fast.",
  "documentReadinessGoalWorkBodyGeneric": "Review what can block early work in the destination: identity consistency, immigration status, and profession-specific proof.",
  "documentReadinessGoalRemoteTitle": "Stabilize the document base for remote income",
  "documentReadinessGoalRemoteBodyBrazil": "Keep tax identity, banking references, and proof that supports contracts, transfers, and a stable routine in Brazil.",
  "documentReadinessGoalRemoteBodyGeneric": "Keep tax identity, banking references, and the proof that supports contracts and international income flow in the new country.",
  "documentReadinessGoalStudyTitle": "Protect the study path with the right records",
  "documentReadinessGoalStudyBodyBrazil": "Keep admissions, school records, identity documents, and timing-sensitive paperwork aligned before relying on study as the entry path.",
  "documentReadinessGoalStudyBodyGeneric": "Keep admissions, school records, identity documents, and timing-sensitive paperwork aligned before relying on study as the base.",
  "documentReadinessGoalEntrepreneurTitle": "Prepare the operating document layer",
  "documentReadinessGoalEntrepreneurBodyBrazil": "Separate the identity, banking, and residency proof that will affect how safely you can start operating once in Brazil.",
  "documentReadinessGoalEntrepreneurBodyGeneric": "Separate the identity, banking, and immigration proof that will affect how safely you can start operating in the destination country.",
  "documentReadinessGoalRetireTitle": "Protect calm arrival with reviewed paperwork",
  "documentReadinessGoalRetireBodyBrazil": "Favor the document set that reduces surprises in health access, banking, and recurring routine once you land in Brazil.",
  "documentReadinessGoalRetireBodyGeneric": "Favor the document set that reduces surprises in health access, banking, and recurring routine once you arrive.",
  "documentReadinessGoalQualityTitle": "Use documents to reduce friction, not just to comply",
  "documentReadinessGoalQualityBodyBrazil": "Even when quality of life is the goal, the smoother move is the one with identity, proof, and arrival paperwork already structured for Brazil.",
  "documentReadinessGoalQualityBodyGeneric": "Even when quality of life is the goal, the smoother move is the one with identity, proof, and arrival paperwork already structured.",
