  "housingEntryPlatformsTitle": "Platforms and useful paths",
  "housingEntryPlatformsHeadline": "Use the right channel for your current risk level",
  "housingEntryPlatformsBody": "The best platform depends less on the pretty listing and more on the bureaucracy you can actually support right now.",
  "housingEntryPlatformsQuintoAndar": "Digital and without a guarantor, but it still expects consistent income and documentation.",
  "housingEntryPlatformsZap": "Use filters like rent without guarantor to cut wasted search time.",
  "housingEntryPlatformsCredPago": "A digital guarantee accepted by many agencies as a guarantor substitute.",
  "housingEntryPlatformsAirbnb": "Useful for the first 15 to 30 days while you visit neighborhoods before taking a longer lease.",
  "housingEntryDisclaimer": "This simulation is directional. Real numbers vary by city, neighborhood, platform, income proof, and landlord policy. The goal is to avoid underestimating the upfront cost.",
  "housingSoftLandingTitle": "How Argentinians usually land before a fixed lease",
  "housingSoftLandingBody": "In the first days, the common path is not going straight into a traditional lease. The sequence is usually landing, temporary housing, and only then the search for a more stable base with less risk.",
  "housingSoftLandingTemporaryTitle": "Land through short stay or serviced flat",
  "housingSoftLandingTemporaryBody": "Monthly Airbnb deals, serviced apartments, and flats help you land without a guarantor or local income proof. That buys time to visit neighborhoods and understand the city in practice.",
  "housingSoftLandingDirectTitle": "Search directly with owners or local groups",
  "housingSoftLandingDirectBody": "Facebook Marketplace, OLX, and direct contacts are often more flexible than a traditional agency. In exchange, scam risk rises and property validation needs to be stricter.",
  "housingSoftLandingGuaranteeTitle": "The exchange currency is the guarantee",
  "housingSoftLandingGuaranteeBody": "Without a guarantor, the strongest argument is usually deposit, guarantee insurance, capitalization title, or a few months paid upfront. The point is not to overpromise, but to arrive with a credible structure.",
  "housingSoftLandingSurvivalTitle": "Arrival survival checklist",
  "housingSoftLandingSurvivalChip": "Buy a Brazilian SIM early. Without a local number, agencies and landlords tend to reply less.",
  "housingSoftLandingSurvivalCpf": "If CPF is not solved yet, treat it as a priority. It matters for platforms, banking, and rental conversations.",
  "housingSoftLandingSurvivalLocation": "In the first days, prioritize staying near groceries, pharmacies, transport, and a health post to reduce cost and friction.",
  "housingSoftLandingSurvivalScam": "Do not send a reservation deposit without visiting the property or having someone you trust verify it locally.",
